T179	Quotation 31415 31518	"And I have some business to do which will take some hours. This business at Coburg Square is serious."
T180	Quotation 31519 31533	"Why serious?"
T181	Quotation 31534 31732	"A considerable crime is in contemplation. I have every reason to believe that we shall be in time to stop it. But to-day being Saturday rather complicates matters. I shall want your help to-night."
T182	Quotation 31733 31748	"At what time?"
T183	Quotation 31749 31776	"Ten will be early enough."
T184	Quotation 31777 31813	"I shall be at Baker Street at ten."
T185	Quotation 31814 31928	"Very well. And, I say, Doctor, there may be some little danger, so kindly put your army revolver in your pocket."
T186	Quotation 33498 33526	"Ha! Our party is complete,"
T187	Cue 33527 33531	said
T188	Entity 33532 33538	Holmes
T189	Quotation 33617 33766	"Watson, I think you know Mr. Jones, of Scotland Yard? Let me introduce you to Mr. Merryweather, who is to be our companion in to-night's adventure."
T190	Quotation 33767 33817	"We're hunting in couples again, Doctor, you see,"
T191	Cue 33818 33822	said
T192	Entity 33823 33828	Jones
T193	Quotation 33855 33975	"Our friend here is a wonderful man for starting a chase. All he wants is an old dog to help him to do the running down.
T194	Quotation 33977 34040	"I hope a wild goose may not prove to be the end of our chase,"
T195	Cue 34041 34049	observed
T196	Entity 34050 34066	Mr. Merryweather
T197	Quotation 34077 34136	"You may place considerable confidence in Mr. Holmes, sir,"
T198	Cue 34137 34141	said
T200	Quotation 34168 34500	"He has his own little methods, which are, if he won't mind my saying so, just a little too theoretical and fantastic, but he has the makings of a detective in him. It is not too much to say that once or twice, as in that business of the Sholto murder and the Agra treasure, he has been more nearly correct than the official force."
T201	Quotation 34501 34549	"Oh, if you say so, Mr. Jones, it is all right,"
T202	Cue 34550 34554	said
T203	Entity 34555 34567	the stranger
T204	Quotation 34584 34714	"Still, I confess that I miss my rubber. It is the first Saturday night for seven-and-twenty years that I have not had my rubber."
T205	Quotation 34715 34739	"I think you will find,"
T206	Cue 34740 34744	said
T207	Entity 34745 34760	Sherlock Holmes
T208	Quotation 34762 35026	"that you will play for a higher stake to-night than you have ever done yet, and that the play will be more exciting. For you, Mr. Merryweather, the stake will beDONEDET53930,000 pounds; and for you, Jones, it will be the man upon whom you wish to lay your hands."
T209	Quotation 35027 35662	"John Clay, the murderer, thief, smasher, and forger. He's a young man, Mr. Merryweather, but he is at the head of his profession, and I would rather have my bracelets on him than on any criminal in London. He's a remarkable man, is young John Clay. His grandfather was a royal duke, and he himself has been to Eton and Oxford. His brain is as cunning as his fingers, and though we meet signs of him at every turn, we never know where to find the man himself. He'll crack a crib in Scotland one week, and be raising money to build an orphanage in Cornwall the next. I've been on his track for years and have never set eyes on him yet."
T210	Quotation 35663 35986	"I hope that I may have the pleasure of introducing you to-night. I've had one or two little turns also with Mr. John Clay, and I agree with you that he is at the head of his profession. It is past ten, however, and quite time that we started. If you two will take the first hansom, Watson and I will follow in the second."
T211	Quotation 36231 36256	"We are close there now,"
T212	Entity 36257 36266	my friend
T213	Cue 36267 36275	remarked
T214	Quotation 36277 36646	"This fellow Merryweather is a bank director, and personally interested in the matter. I thought it as well to have Jones with us also. He is not a bad fellow, though an absolute imbecile in his profession. He has one positive virtue. He is as brave as a bulldog and as tenacious as a lobster if he gets his claws upon anyone. Here we are, and they are waiting for us."
T215	Quotation 37310 37351	"You are not very vulnerable from above,"
T216	Entity 37352 37358	Holmes
T217	Cue 37359 37367	remarked
T218	Quotation 37415 37432	"Nor from below,"
T219	Cue 37433 37437	said
T220	Entity 37438 37454	Mr. Merryweather
T221	Quotation 37513 37552	"Why, dear me, it sounds quite hollow!"
T222	Entity 37553 37555	he
T223	Cue 37556 37564	remarked
T224	Quotation 37590 37640	"I must really ask you to be a little more quiet!"
T225	Cue 37641 37645	said
T226	Entity 37646 37652	Holmes
T227	Quotation 37663 37833	"You have already imperilled the whole success of our expedition. Might I beg that you would have the goodness to sit down upon one of those boxes, and not to interfere?"
T228	Quotation 38192 38229	"We have at least an hour before us,"
T229	Quotation 38243 38770	"for they can hardly take any steps until the good pawnbroker is safely in bed. Then they will not lose a minute, for the sooner they do their work the longer time they will have for their escape. We are at present, Doctor-- as no doubt you have divined-- in the cellar of the City branch of one of the principal London banks. Mr. Merryweather is the chairman of directors, and he will explain to you that there are reasons why the more daring criminals of London should take a considerable interest in this cellar at present."
T230	Cue 38233 38241	remarked
T231	Quotation 38771 38795	"It is our French gold,"
T232	Cue 38796 38805	whispered
T233	Entity 38806 38818	the director
T234	Quotation 38820 38889	"We have had several warnings that an attempt might be made upon it."
T235	Quotation 38890 38909	"Your French gold?"
T236	Quotation 38910 39404	"Yes. We had occasion some months ago to strengthen our resources and borrowed for that purpose 30,000 napoleons from the Bank of France. It has become known that we have never had occasion to unpack the money, and that it is still lying in our cellar. The crate upon which I sit contains 2,000 napoleons packed between layers of lead foil. Our reserve of bullion is much larger at present than is usually kept in a single branch office, and the directors have had misgivings upon the subject."
T237	Quotation 39405 39438	"Which were very well justified,"
T238	Cue 39439 39447	observed
T239	Entity 39448 39454	Holmes
T240	Quotation 39456 39650	"And now it is time that we arranged our little plans. I expect that within an hour matters will come to a head. In the meantime Mr. Merryweather, we must put the screen over that dark lantern."
T241	Quotation 39651 39673	"And sit in the dark?"
T242	Quotation 39674 40292	"I am afraid so. I had brought a pack of cards in my pocket, and I thought that, as we were a partie carrée, you might have your rubber after all. But I see that the enemy's preparations have gone so far that we cannot risk the presence of a light. And, first of all, we must choose our positions. These are daring men, and though we shall take them at a disadvantage, they may do us some harm unless we are careful. I shall stand behind this crate, and do you conceal yourselves behind those. Then, when I flash a light upon them, close in swiftly. If they fire, Watson, have no compunction about shooting them down."
T243	Quotation 40808 40836	"They have but one retreat,"
T244	Cue 40837 40846	whispered
T245	Entity 40847 40853	Holmes
T246	Quotation 40855 40963	"That is back through the house into Saxe-Coburg Square. I hope that you have done what I asked you, Jones?"
T247	Quotation 40964 41029	"I have an inspector and two officers waiting at the front door."
T248	Quotation 41030 41103	"Then we have stopped all the holes. And now we must be silent and wait."
T249	Quotation 42866 42883	"It's all clear,"
T250	Entity 42884 42886	he
T251	Cue 42887 42896	whispered
T252	Quotation 42898 42989	"Have you the chisel and the bags? Great Scott! Jump, Archie, jump, and I'll swing for it!"
T253	Quotation 43312 43337	"It's no use, John Clay,"
T254	Cue 43338 43342	said
T255	Entity 43343 43349	Holmes
T256	Quotation 43359 43387	"You have no chance at all."
T257	Quotation 43388 43399	"So I see,"
T258	Entity 43400 43409	the other
T259	Cue 43410 43418	answered
T260	Quotation 43445 43522	"I fancy that my pal is all right, though I see you have got his coat-tails."
T261	Quotation 43523 43573	"There are three men waiting for him at the door,"
T262	Cue 43574 43578	said
T263	Entity 43579 43585	Holmes
T264	Quotation 43587 43672	"Oh, indeed! You seem to have done the thing very completely. I must compliment you."
T265	Quotation 43673 43685	"And I you,"
T266	Entity 43686 43692	Holmes
T267	Cue 43693 43701	answered
T268	Quotation 43703 43753	"Your red-headed idea was very new and effective."
T269	Quotation 43754 43792	"You'll see your pal again presently,"
T270	Cue 43793 43797	said
T271	Entity 43798 43803	Jones
T272	Quotation 43805 43892	"He's quicker at climbing down holes than I am. Just hold out while I fix the derbies."
T273	Quotation 43893 43951	"I beg that you will not touch me with your filthy hands,"
T274	Cue 43952 43960	remarked
T275	Entity 43961 43973	our prisoner
T276	Quotation 44018 44156	"You may not be aware that I have royal blood in my veins. Have the goodness, also, when you address me always to say 'sir' and 'please.'"
T277	Quotation 44157 44169	"All right,"
T278	Cue 44170 44174	said
T279	Entity 44175 44180	Jones
T280	Quotation 44209 44324	"Well, would you please, sir, march upstairs, where we can get a cab to carry your Highness to the police-station?"
T281	Quotation 44325 44342	"That is better,"
T282	Cue 44343 44347	said
T283	Entity 44348 44357	John Clay
T284	Quotation 44466 44487	"Really, Mr. Holmes,"
T285	Cue 44488 44492	said
T286	Entity 44493 44509	Mr. Merryweather
T287	Quotation 44547 44779	"I do not know how the bank can thank you or repay you. There is no doubt that you have detected and defeated in the most complete manner one of the most determined attempts at bank robbery that have ever come within my experience."
T288	Quotation 44780 44857	"I have had one or two little scores of my own to settle with Mr. John Clay,"
T289	Cue 44858 44862	said
T290	Entity 44863 44869	Holmes
T291	Quotation 44871 45128	"I have been at some small expense over this matter, which I shall expect the bank to refund, but beyond that I am amply repaid by having had an experience which is in many ways unique, and by hearing the very remarkable narrative of the Red-headed League."
T292	Quotation 45129 45147	"You see, Watson,"
T293	Entity 45148 45150	he
T294	Cue 45151 45160	explained
T295	Quotation 45254 46178	"it was perfectly obvious from the first that the only possible object of this rather fantastic business of the advertisement of the League, and the copying of the 'Encyclopaedia,' must be to get this not over-bright pawnbroker out of the way for a number of hours every day. It was a curious way of managing it, but, really, it would be difficult to suggest a better. The method was no doubt suggested to Clay's ingenious mind by the colour of his accomplice's hair.DONEDET7414 pounds a week was a lure which must draw him, and what was it to them, who were playing for thousands? They put in the advertisement, one rogue has the temporary office, the other rogue incites the man to apply for it, and together they manage to secure his absence every morning in the week. From the time that I heard of the assistant having come for half wages, it was obvious to me that he had some strong motive for securing the situation."
T296	Quotation 46179 46225	"But how could you guess what the motive was?"
T297	Quotation 46226 47959	"Had there been women in the house, I should have suspected a mere vulgar intrigue. That, however, was out of the question. The man's business was a small one, and there was nothing in his house which could account for such elaborate preparations, and such an expenditure as they were at. It must, then, be something out of the house. What could it be? I thought of the assistant's fondness for photography, and his trick of vanishing into the cellar. The cellar! There was the end of this tangled clue. Then I made inquiries as to this mysterious assistant and found that I had to deal with one of the coolest and most daring criminals in London. He was doing something in the cellar-- something which took many hours a day for months on end. What could it be, once more? I could think of nothing save that he was running a tunnel to some other building.  So far I had got when we went to visit the scene of action. I surprised you by beating upon the pavement with my stick. I was ascertaining whether the cellar stretched out in front or behind. It was not in front. Then I rang the bell, and, as I hoped, the assistant answered it. We have had some skirmishes, but we had never set eyes upon each other before. I hardly looked at his face. His knees were what I wished to see. You must yourself have remarked how worn, wrinkled, and stained they were. They spoke of those hours of burrowing. The only remaining point was what they were burrowing for. I walked round the corner, saw the City and Suburban Bank abutted on our friend's premises, and felt that I had solved my problem. When you drove home after the concert I called upon Scotland Yard and upon the chairman of the bank directors, with the result that you have seen."
T298	Quotation 47960 48029	"And how could you tell that they would make their attempt to-night?"
T299	Entity 48030 48031	I
T300	Cue 48032 48037	asked
T301	Quotation 48039 48484	"Well, when they closed their League offices that was a sign that they cared no longer about Mr. Jabez Wilson's presence-- in other words, that they had completed their tunnel. But it was essential that they should use it soon, as it might be discovered, or the bullion might be removed. Saturday would suit them better than any other day, as it would give them two days for their escape. For all these reasons I expected them to come to-night."
T302	Quotation 48485 48519	"You reasoned it out beautifully,"
T303	Entity 48520 48521	I
T304	Cue 48522 48531	exclaimed
T305	Quotation 48557 48612	"It is so long a chain, and yet every link rings true."
T306	Quotation 48613 48638	"It saved me from ennui,"
T307	Entity 48639 48641	he
T308	Cue 48642 48650	answered
T309	Quotation 48661 48828	"Alas! I already feel it closing in upon me. My life is spent in one long effort to escape from the commonplaces of existence. These little problems help me to do so."
T310	Quotation 48829 48868	"And you are a benefactor of the race,"
T311	Cue 48869 48873	said
T312	Entity 48874 48875	I
T313	Quotation 48904 48957	"Well, perhaps, after all, it is of some little use,"
T314	Entity 48958 48960	he
T315	Cue 48961 48969	remarked
T316	Quotation 48971 49058	"'L'homme c'est rien-- l'oeuvre c'est tout,' as Gustave Flaubert wrote to George Sand."
